      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "More than 7,200 British women have endometrial cancer diagnosed every year. It is a figure that is rising markedly, with the cancer being linked to problems with obesity on an international scale. Although an early diagnosis leads to a good prognosis, after treatment has been completed patients are asked to attend regular outpatient clinic appointments for three to five years."},
